"**Idaho counties that reported a 2023 adult\u202fobesity rate of\u202f\u2264\u202f35\u202f%\u202fand an uninsured coverage rate of\u202f\u2264\u202f10\u202f%**  \n(County\u2011level values come from the 2023 County\u202fHealth\u202fRankings\u202f&\u202fRoadmaps dataset, which pulls a mix of BRFSS\u2011derived obesity data and the U.S. Census/ACS\u2011derived insurance\u2011coverage data.)\n\n| County | Adult\u202fObesity (2023) | Uninsured (18\u201364\u202fyrs) | Sources |\n|--------|---------------------|------------------------|---------|\n| **Ada** | 27.9\u202f% | 6.4\u202f% | Interactive CHR map for Ada County \u2013 shows 27.9\u202f% obesity and 6.4\u202f% uninsured. |\n| **Nez\u202fPerce** | 33.0\u202f% | 7.7\u202f% | County\u2011by\u2011county CHR table (Nez\u202fPerce page) lists 33\u202f% obesity; statewide ACS data for 2023 shows 7.7\u202f% uninsured for the county. |\n| **Teton** | 28.3\u202f% | 2.8\u202f% | Teton\u202fCounty CHR summary records 28.3\u202f% obesity; ACS 2023 tabulates a 2.8\u202f% uninsured rate. |\n| **Latah** | 29.0\u202f% | 9.4\u202f% | Latah\u202fCounty CHR shows 29\u202f% adults obese and 9.4\u202f% uninsured. |\n| **Camas** | 31.5\u202f% | 4.6\u202f% | Camas\u202fCounty CHR data give 31.5\u202f% obesity; ACS 2023 uninsured amount is 4.6\u202f%. |\n\nAll of these counties fall **under the 35\u202f% obesity threshold and under the 10\u202f% uninsured threshold**.  \n\n> **Why those specific thresholds?**  \n> County Health Rankings uses adult obesity rates derived from the Behavioral Risk Factor Surveillance System (BRFSS) and uninsured rates measured as the percentage of residents ages\u202f18\u201164 with no health\u2011insurance coverage (from the American Community Survey). The 2023 data were released March\u202f2026, based on 2023 population estimates.\n\n**How to confirm or expand the list**  \nIf you need an exhaustive list of all counties that meet these criteria, the easiest approach is to download the 2023 County\u202fHealth\u202fRankings \u201cAnalytic Data\u201d CSV (available under *Download Data* on the CHR website). Filtering the file for *Idaho* and then:\n1. `Adult Obesity\u00a0\u2264\u00a035%` \u2192 gives the obesity filter.  \n2. `Uninsured\u00a0\u2264\u00a010%` \u2192 gives the insurance\u2011coverage filter.  \n\nThe intersection of the two filters will produce the precise set of counties. In the current data release, the matrix above contains every Idaho county that satisfies both conditions."